-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Why NonCommercial
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Parts of this repository are derived from Meta's Masked Autoencoders (MAE) and
MAE-ST, which are released under CC BY-NC 4.0. That license is inherited by the
files listed below, and it is the reason this repository as a whole is
NonCommercial rather than permissive.


-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party components
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This repository incorporates code from the following projects. Their original
licenses continue to apply to the corresponding files.

  MAE / MAE-ST (Meta Platforms, Inc.)          CC BY-NC 4.0
      https://github.com/facebookresearch/mae
      https://github.com/facebookresearch/mae_st
      util/misc.py, util/pos_embed.py, util/lr_sched.py, util/video_vit.py,
      model/models_vit_tensor.py

  SpectralGPT (Hong et al., IEEE TPAMI)
      https://github.com/danfenghong/IEEE_TPAMI_SpectralGPT
      The ViT backbone and its pretrained initialisation.

  MMST-ViT (Fudong Lin et al.)                 MIT
      https://github.com/fudong03/MMST-ViT
      attention.py (spatial / temporal / multi-modal transformers),
      model/models_PhenoYieldNet.py, dataset/*_loader.py, dataset/*_wrapper.py,
      util/cnn_modules.py, configs/build_config_multicrop.py

  Latent Diffusion (CompVis)                   MIT
      https://github.com/CompVis/latent-diffusion
      attention.py: GEGLU, FeedForward, PreNorm and the helper functions.

  Autoformer / FEDformer                       MIT
      https://github.com/thuml/Autoformer
      attention.py: moving_avg, series_decomp_multi.

  SimCLR (Thalles Silva)                       MIT
      https://github.com/sthalles/SimCLR
      loss/contrastive_loss.py.

  timm (Ross Wightman)                         Apache-2.0
      https://github.com/huggingface/pytorch-image-models
      Used as a dependency.
